Here is the complete source code and documentation for Charter, a family-office governance platform from The Harris Office, designed for the fictional Ashford family of Houston.

Architecture Overview
To keep the codebase straightforward and easily extensible for another engineer, the project uses React 18, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS via Vite with zero heavy external state libraries:

src/types/charter.ts: Strongly typed domain models (Responsibility, Decision, GivingRecord) and shared status types.

src/data/seedData.ts: Realistic fictional baseline data for the Ashford family across three generations (Arthur & Eleanor, Julian & Claire, Maya & Leo), covering Ashford Energy Holdings, the Ashford Family Foundation, their River Oaks and Aspen properties, and their Post-War American art collection.

src/hooks/useCharterStore.ts: A single custom hook managing localStorage persistence, CRUD operations, cross-section links, toast notifications, and the demo data reset flow.

src/components/: Modular, single-responsibility UI components styled with a calm, editorial palette (warm ivory #FAF8F4, deep maroon #5C1D2A, and slate periwinkle #4A609A).
